{"data":{"id":6945,"name":"Amp","symbol":"AMP","slug":"amp","category":"token","description":"## What Is Amp (AMP)?\n\nAmp is an open-source digital collateral token designed to support fast and efficient transfers of value. When used as collateral, Amp allows transactions to be guaranteed and settle instantly, even while the underlying asset completes final settlement.\n\nAmp is held in escrow by collateral managers during a transfer and released once the transaction successfully settles. This enables speed without compromising settlement assurance.\n\nNetworks such as Flexa use Amp to secure real-world payments and other value transfer use cases.\n\nAmp uses collateral managers and token partitions to support flexible collateralization. Token partitions allow Amp to be assigned as collateral without transferring tokens to another address, while collateral managers control how collateral is locked and released.\n\nThrough this structure, Amp serves as universal collateral for applications that require reliable and efficient value transfers.\n\n\n\n## Who Are the Founders of Amp?\n\nAmp's parent company is Flexa, a blockchain payments company based in New York that specializes in FinTech and builds a future with more efficient, secure and affordable real-world payments. Flexa was co-founded in 2018 by Tyler Spalding, Trevor Filter, Daniel McCabe and Zachary Kilgore.\n\n\n## What Makes Amp (AMP) Unique?\n\nAmp enables instant payments worldwide by guaranteeing the value of a transaction.\n\nAmp uses a flexible collateral system that secures value transfers without intermediaries or changes to the underlying asset. This allows Flexa to complete payments instantly at the point of sale, even if the digital asset itself takes minutes or hours to settle on chain.\n\nCollateral managers can be customized for different applications, and token partitions allow Amp to be assigned as collateral without moving tokens from their original address. This means value can be guaranteed without custody risk, delays, or added complexity for users.\n\nIn simple terms, Amp removes settlement risk. It ensures the merchant is paid immediately, no matter what asset is being spent or how long final settlement takes.\n\nThat is what makes Amp uniquely suited for Flexa and why it can power instant, final digital payments at global scale.\n\n\n### Related Pages:\n\nLearn more about Flexa in [Flexa: The Pure-Digital Payments Network](https://www.gemini.com/cryptopedia/flexa-crypto-amp-token).\n\nVisit the official [Flexa website](https://flexa.co/).\n\nExplore community [explainers and breakdowns](https://x.com/floatingratio/status/1532288513059835905).\n\nWhat are collateral tokens? Find out with the [CMC glossary](https://coinmarketcap.com/alexandria/glossary/collateral-tokens).\n\nLearn more about the crypto space with our [educational section](https://coinmarketcap.com/alexandria).\n\n\n## How Many Amp (AMP) Coins Are There in Circulation?\n\nThe AMP token is deployed on the Ethereum blockchain as an [ERC-20](https://coinmarketcap.com/alexandria/glossary/erc-20) token.\n\nAt the time of writing, there are over 84B $AMP (84%) in circulation, out of a maximum supply of 99,720,006,935 coins. To reduce the risk of volatility, AMP’s supply is fixed and non-inflationary.\n\n\n## How Is the Amp Network Secured?\n\nAMP is built on Ethereum's blockchain, which is secured by a [proof-of-stake](https://coinmarketcap.com/alexandria/glossary/proof-of-stake-pos) (PoS) consensus mechanism. The Amp smart contracts have been audited by ConsenSys Diligence and Trail of Bits.\n\n\n## Where Can You Buy Amp (AMP)?\n\nAmp (AMP) is currently available on [Binance](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/binance/), [Coinbase Exchange](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/coinbase-exchange/), [KuCoin](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/kucoin/), [Uniswap](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/uniswap-v2/), [Gemini](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/gemini/), [SushiSwap](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/sushiswap/), [Bittrex](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/bittrex/), [Huobi](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/huobi/), [Gate.io](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/gate-io/), [Crypto.com Exchange](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/crypto-com-exchange/), [LBank](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/lbank/), [Bitrue](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/bitrue/), [WhiteBIT](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/whitebit/), [XT.COM](https://coinmarketcap.com/exchanges/xt/) and more.\n\nWant to keep track of AMP prices live? Download the [CMC mobile app](https://coinmarketcap.com/mobile/).\n\nExpand your knowledge of crypto with [CMC Alexandria](https://coinmarketcap.com/alexandria).","dateAdded":"2020-09-08T00:00:00.000Z","actualTimeStart":"2020-09-11T04:30:00.000Z","status":"active","isBn":1,"subStatus":"normal","notice":"","alertType":2,"alertLink":"","latestUpdateTime":"2026-10-19T06:42:00.000Z","watchCount":"221809","watchListRanking":208,"dateLaunched":"2020-09-06T00:00:00.000Z","latestAdded":false,"launchPrice":0.00952341,"tags":[{"slug":"ethereum-ecosystem","name":"Ethereum Ecosystem","category":"PLATFORM","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"alleged-sec-securities","name":"Alleged SEC Securities","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"made-in-america","name":"Made in America","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"binance-ecosystem","name":"Binance Ecosystem","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":5},{"slug":"binance-listing","name":"Binance Listing","category":"CATEGORY","status":0,"priority":5}],"selfReportedTags":["DeFi","Payments"],"selfReportedCirculatingSupply":"84231571807.15","urls":{"website":["https://amp.xyz"],"technical_doc":["https://4079620000-files.gitbook.io/~/files/v0/b/gitbook-x-prod.appspot.com/o/spaces%2FbUyUOpvS5Hnfel4aMnVz%2Fuploads%2F8ZKNS6MmVMUQaiN2BidF%2FAmp%20Whitepaper.pdf?alt=media&token=66f22011-0b4c-42d7-8a2c-17eaea145ee1"],"explorer":["https://etherscan.io/token/0xff